=== Text #12 ===
> I think this is one of the most interesting pieces of researching in epidemiology and profound effects on society I have ever seen. I wrote about Kevin Drum’s original work on the connection between lead in the environment and crime rates (I’m not linking to my piece, his piece is linked to in the Brookings piece). This is one of those things where the evidence is so clear, but the conclusion just seems too easy, that contingents in sociology believe it too good to be true.
I think it’s fascinating, your mileage may vary.[][][][][][][][][][][][][][][][]

=== Text #13 ===
> Nov 15, 2018 in "Guardians of the Galaxy"
Disney has today released new artwork of the ride vehicles that will be part of the new Guardians of the Galaxy coaster coming to Epcot in 2021.
Disney Parks, Experiences and Consumer Products Chairman Bob Ch[ape]k said, “On most coasters, the vehicles point straight ahead[ throughout] the ride,” Bob explained. “But[ on] this attraction, each individual cab will be programmed to direct your eye to the story happening around you.[][][][][][][][][][][][][][]

=== Text #14 ===
> My idea is more of creating an endless loop. A duckling will[ al]way follow either its mother or another duckling. By scaring the mother she turns around and you create the first part[ of] the loop. If you take away the mother in the right moment, the first duckling will see the last duckling and follow it. So the loop is closed. After seeing this comic I[ real]y would like to test it in reality.[ But I] think the sound of the mother will ruin everthing (shout out warnings).
